<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · Egypt, North Africa and Sudan</p><h1 class="st-title">Fifteenth Dynasty of Egypt</h1><p class="st-meta">1650 BCE – 1550 BCE (approx.) · capital Avaris</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The Hyksos kings of Avaris, rulers of Levantine origin who governed northern Egypt for about a century.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Around 1650 BCE rulers of Levantine descent, called <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hyksos">Hyksos</a> from the Egyptian for 'rulers of foreign lands', took power at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/avaris">Avaris</a> in the eastern Delta and captured <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/memphis-egypt">Memphis</a>, ending the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/middle-kingdom-of-egypt">Middle Kingdom of Egypt</a>. Later Egyptian tradition portrayed this as an invasion, but it grew from a long-settled Canaanite population in the Delta.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hyksos">Hyksos</a> adopted pharaonic titles and Egyptian administration while keeping Levantine customs at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/avaris">Avaris</a>, where their great palaces and temples have been excavated. They worshipped <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seth">Seth</a>, identified with the storm god <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baal">Baal</a>, and traded widely with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/canaan">Canaan</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cyprus">Cyprus</a>. Their era spread the horse and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chariot">chariot</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a>, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rhind-mathematical-papyrus">Rhind Mathematical Papyrus</a> was copied under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/apepi">Apepi</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khyan">Khyan's</a> name appears on objects found as far as <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/palace-state-of-knossos">Knossos</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baghdad">Baghdad</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/seventeenth-dynasty-of-egypt">Seventeenth Dynasty of Egypt</a> at <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/thebes">Thebes</a> went to war against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/apepi">Apepi</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ahmose-i">Ahmose I</a>, who came to the throne around 1550 BCE, captured <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/avaris">Avaris</a> some years later and then besieged <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sharuhen">Sharuhen</a> in southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/canaan">Canaan</a>, driving out the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hyksos">Hyksos</a> and founding the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/egyptian-empire-new-kingdom">Egyptian Empire New Kingdom</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/fifteenth-dynasty-of-egypt.jpg" alt="Fifteenth Dynasty of Egypt" width="320" height="653"><figcaption>Image: Iry-Hor · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Egypt_Hyksos_Period.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1650 BCE – 1550 BCE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/17th-century-bce">17th century BCE</a> – <a href="/centuries/16th-century-bce">16th century BCE</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Avaris</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Khyan, Apepi</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Ancient Egyptian religion, Canaanite religion</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Egyptian, Amorite</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/egypt">Egypt</a>, <a href="/countries/israel">Israel</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Hyksos, Hyksos Dynasty, Fifteenth Dynasty</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=-1600&amp;focus=fifteenth-dynasty-of-egypt" aria-label="Fifteenth Dynasty of Egypt on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5504 1055 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Fifteenth Dynasty of Egypt lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5824 1311L5863 1489M5824 1311L